      "content": "It's natural to feel that way when you've invested so much only to have it vanish; the exhaustion of that kind of loss is overwhelming. Instead of viewing it as starting from zero, maybe consider what parts of your drive or skills still exist within you. You have decades of experience, even if the structure around it is gone, and that experience is still valuable. Focus on small, manageable steps forward, even if they don't feel like a grand rebuild right now.",
